Description: In a 3D project every effect and composition acts on each eye
 MLT gives every filter and transition each eye of a frame of two eyes as a
 picture of its own (MLT 0019), so an effect's or composition's rectangle,
 crop, rotation or blur is in one eye's coordinates, as in a 2D project of the
 project's size. The render keeps the document's profile of one eye: each
 clip's stereo3d_unpack makes the frame of two profile-sized views
 (pair_frame), and the consumer, given a profile of its own (scale), asks for
 twice the width; before, the whole document's profile was doubled and every
 geometry was measured against the frame of two eyes. The timeline preview's
 chunks of a 3D project are prepared and rendered the same way (the chunk
 consumer of kdenlive_render has a profile of its own) and played back marked
 as frames of two eyes. A clip already in the project's pair shape keeps its
 filter (MLT hands it on as it is), so its effects act on each eye too. An
 effect that MLT can only run on the two eyes as one picture (it keeps earlier
 pictures and moves what it shows or reaches over neighbouring samples) says so
 in its panel in a 3D project.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
